[h2]0.1[/h2]
[b]First release.[/b] An add-on for [b]Detailed Map Tacks[/b] by wltk - it patches that mod and does nothing without it.
[list]
[*] [b]Generic map tacks are now cleared when what they stand for gets built.[/b] Detailed Map Tacks removes a pin when the building it names is finished on that plot, but the check compares the two type names as text - so it only ever matched a pin for one specific building. A "culture building" or "wonder" pin could never match anything and stayed on the map for the rest of the game. It now disappears as soon as a building that fulfils it goes up, using the same list of buildings the pin's own tooltip shows you.
[*] [b]Right-click a map tack on the map to delete it.[/b] Detailed Map Tacks on its own only deletes a tack on left-click, and only while the tack chooser is open. The click is swallowed, so it does not also send your selected unit walking to that tile. New option [b]Remove map tacks with right-click[/b], on by default.
[*] Walls and other slotless buildings do not clear a pin, and a unique quarter pin waits for both of its buildings - a plan is only cleared when it is actually finished.
[*] Requires Detailed Map Tacks. Declared as a hard dependency, so the fixes simply do not apply if that mod is missing or switched off.
[*] New option under Options - Mods: [b]Apply Detailed Map Tacks fixes[/b], on by default. Turns every fix off without uninstalling this mod - the first thing to try if map tacks misbehave after a Detailed Map Tacks update.
[*] Available in twelve languages.
[/list]
